    "created_at": "2025-07-27T08:40:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-27T08:40:02Z",
    "body": "> The `class=\"\"` attribute can be used for domain-specific concepts like \"ledes\".\n\nThis question is to do with the semantics of identifying this for processing on the server side, this has nothing to do with stylesheets.\n\nTo clarify, the lede is \"the opening sentence or paragraph of a news article, summarizing the most important aspects of the story.\". In other words, the lede is a property of an article described by the article tag.\n\nGiven that multiple article tags can exist, I will go with the first paragraph after the main tag.\n\nhtml/body/main/p\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
